WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.393
"Ginkgo Biloba as a Brain Health Supplement for Dementia"

00:00:07.393 --> 00:00:09.341
More than a third
of older Americans

00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:12.000
take some kind
of brain health supplement

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.517
to the tune
of billions of dollars a year,

00:00:15.517 --> 00:00:19.020
and one of the most popular
is ginkgo biloba.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.300
U.S. household surveys suggest

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.800
as many as 2 percent
of Americans

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.780
are taking gingko supplements.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.840
Ginkgo biloba's a tree
with fan-shaped leaves,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.060
regarded as a living fossil,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.400
having persisted
relatively unchanged

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.560
for over
a quarter billion years.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.100
Its resilience makes it
a favorite of urban planners,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.240
hardy enough to survive
even a nuclear blast,

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.880
as one of the few survivors
within a short radius

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.680
of ground zero in Hiroshima.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.300
Over the last 30 years or so,
an extract of gingko leaves

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.000
has become one of the most
widely used herbal treatments

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.380
for dementia.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.660
A 2009 Cochrane review

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.900
of three dozen
randomized controlled trials

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.420
involving more than
4,000 participants

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.180
concluded that
the "evidence that ginkgo biloba

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.400
has predictable and clinically
significant benefit

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.560
for people with dementia
or cognitive impairment

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.260
is inconsistent
and unreliable."

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.140
One trial showed
very large benefits,

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.540
but others showed
no effect at all.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.200
To put the subject to rest
once and for all,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.360
two large randomized,
double-blind,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.180
placebo-controlled trials
were conducted, one in Europe,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.640
funded by a gingko
supplement manufacturer,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.800
and the largest,
longest study to date,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.440
funded by the NIH
in the United States.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.680
More than 5,000
older men and women

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.280
with either normal cognition
or mild cognitive impairment

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.520
were randomized to
a gingko leaf extract or placebo

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.820
for five or six years
to see if it would prevent them

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.460
from sliding into dementia.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.260
Mild cognitive impairment

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.480
is the intermediate
clinical state

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.720
between normal cognition
for one's age and dementia.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.680
The conversion rate
of MCI to dementia

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.660
is about 10 percent per year.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.340
The bottom line?

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:09.300
Neither trial
showed any clear benefit,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.080
definitively demonstrating
no preventative effect.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.060
However, for those
already suffering with dementia,

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.720
gingko leaf extracts do appear
to slow cognitive decline

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.360
compared to placebo
for those with Alzheimer's,

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.000
or dementia
more broadly defined.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.660
Of course that's assuming
there's actually gingko

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.280
in your gingko supplements.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.800
Investigations
of gingko supplements

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.140
off the shelves
in both Europe and the U.S.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:40.560
found some that had
no apparent gingko at all.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.740
As high as about
one in six ginkgo supplements

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.240
appeared to be all filler,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.240
without any detectable
ginkgo biloba DNA.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.260
Side-effects-wise,
at typical doses,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.240
such as 120 mg twice a day,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.300
ginkgo extracts may cause
mild stomach upset,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.820
headache, dizziness,
constipation,

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.860
and allergic skin reactions.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:05.160
Higher dosages can result
in restlessness, diarrhea,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.900
nausea, vomiting, and weakness.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.660
There have been about a dozen
published case reports

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.820
of bleeding
associated with gingko,

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.040
but thankfully
this did not surface

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.980
in systematic reviews
of the dementia studies.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:19.200
Still, out of
an abundance of caution,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.260
it's been recommended to
stop taking gingko supplements

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.260
at least two weeks
before elective surgery.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.860
The bottom line,
according to a recent review

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.600
of Alzheimer's disease
therapies,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.580
is that ginkgo
is one of the few things

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.640
that can beat out placebo
for cognitive function.

